              "type": "reasoning.summary",
              "summary": "**Evaluating trophy design**\n\nIt seems like creating a feasible concept is tricky, particularly with sparse and strict artificial guidelines. I'm brainstorming a possible 5-hop structure starting from the official event to the trophy design. Maybe we could go from the event's visual identity to a title for a plaque. \n\nI’m also considering a physical trophy based on an eagle, since the design needs to avoid features like rooster combs. In my memory, the Golden Eagle Award trophy might feature a female figure holding a golden eagle.**Designing award visuals**\n\nI'm picturing the trophy for the China Golden Eagle TV Arts Festival as possibly a golden eagle with spread wings on a rectangular base. I need to distinguish between the \"金鹰女神\" statue and the trophy itself. The statue could represent a goddess figure with arms raised and eagle wings behind her, which is iconic. For the trophy, I could incorporate text like \"金鹰奖\" on both the nominee envelopes and the official plaque. I'm considering using a live feed for a polished look, avoiding mirrors to keep it authentic.**Planning award ceremony visuals**\n\nI’m considering how to syncronize repeated text and count for the live screen during the award ceremony. The idea of having text displayed in a screen-in-screen format sounds interesting. I could use a custom term like \"实时转播\" or something more concise like \"屏幕转播.\" \n\nThis setup would work well for a televised award event, featuring one male winner, two presenters, and the Golden Eagle trophy. I want to ensure the giant LED screen shows real-time close-ups and captures the ideal angles of everything happening on stage.",
